From 85f70c8494d18e8b01e6a21172492ab6cc92ded8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:38:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban release: prove delayed legacy comment refs
 from retained receipts

Manual unblock/promote of long-lived cards (retention final owner
t_5f0d878cd1c10371, source owner t_0b716b01a47db7f6) refused forever with
"Comment data unavailable ... --seen cannot acknowledge missing data", even
though every comment row was readable.

Five whys:
1. --seen checks every historical commented event, not just recent ones.
2. Legacy events without comment_uid fall back to a +/-1 s row match.
3. Observed rows were stamped 2-13 s before their event (e.g. hub event
   1087059 -> comment 190729, +13 s), so the fallback finds nothing.
4. The old producer omitted the portable comment_uid, and PR #3297 only
   bridges delays for proven *local writer runs*; interactive/subagent
   no-run comments have no such provenance.
5. Tests covered near-time imports and delayed local runs, not no-run
   delayed writers.

Fix: when an event stays unresolved and lacks comment_uid, read the writer
session's retained transcript read-only (local state.db, mode=ro) and accept
one receiver row only when ALL hold:
- exactly one successful top-level {ok, task_id, comment_id} receipt for
  this task and source integer exists in the transcript (a second,
  conflicting receipt refuses even when its body never reached the receiver);
- its call ID is declared exactly once across every assistant message and
  tool (checked before any task/body filtering) and replied to exactly once;
- the declaration is a direct kanban_comment call for the same task, with no
  board argument or the checking board's slug;
- the event lies within floor(call)..floor(result); no lateness tolerance;
- exactly one receiver row has that exact stripped body and author within
  that interval.
Anything else, including unreadable/pruned/over-cap transcripts, malformed
declarations, wrapped tool_call batches, cross_task actions and redacted
bodies, stays "data unavailable". Unseen-comment refusal, the injective
coverage matching and every existing resolution path are unchanged; the
proof never writes and never mutates board evidence.

Tests: RED 16 failing (F1 duplicate-declaration borrowing, F2 conflicting
receipts, board namespace, guard-level high-watermark acknowledgement on
promote/unblock/tool); GREEN 159 passed across the transcript + release
suites, 348 passed across 12 adjacent unblock/release consumer suites.
